# Vulnerability details

## Impact

In case stETH is not pegged to ETH with 1:1 ratio, the `LybraStETHVault.sol` will still store all deposits in ETH value after converting to stETH.

Also, the emitted event does not return the received stETH amount `sharesAmount`, but `msg.value` twice. This might confuse the users.

## Proof of Concept

According to [Lido source code](https://etherscan.io/address/0x17144556fd3424edc8fc8a4c940b2d04936d17eb#code), the `submit` function deposits the amount of shares that corresponds to the "protocol-controlled Ether". The code for calculating the amount of stETH in [StETH.sol:300](https://etherscan.io/address/0x17144556fd3424edc8fc8a4c940b2d04936d17eb#code#F27#L300): 
```
_ethAmount.mul(_getTotalShares()).div(_getTotalPooledEther());
```

This means, Lido does not convert the exact `msg.value` ETH amount to stETH with a 1:1 ratio (`msg.value != sharesAmount`).

