## Recommended Mitigation Steps
To fix this, you could add a require statement to the withdraw function that checks the user's balance and only allows them to withdraw up to the amount of tokens that they have staked. For example, the following code would add this check:



function withdraw(uint256 _amount) external updateReward(msg.sender) {
    require(_amount > 0, "amount = 0");
    require(balanceOf[msg.sender] >= _amount, "Not enough balance");
    balanceOf[msg.sender] -= _amount;
    totalSupply -= _amount;
    stakingToken.transfer(msg.sender, _amount);
    emit WithdrawToken(msg.sender, _amount, block.timestamp);
}




This would ensure that a user could never withdraw more tokens than they have staked, which would help to protect the contract from security vulnerabilities.





