In `liquidation()/superLiquidation()` there are missing checks to ensure that liquidator has indeed assigned a keeper and granted access to borrow and collateral balance. This allows anybody to act as a keeper by calling `liquidation()/superLiquidation()` in place of liquidators and earn keeper rewards based on keeper ratio set for pools. 

As long as allowance has been set for vault contracts and liquidator has sufficient collateral and borrow balance, then anybody can act as a keeper and call `liquidation()/superLiquidation` on behalf of liquidator. This causes a slight decrease in collateral returned for liquidator providers depending on keeper reward ratio set, but allow anyone that is not assigned a keeper to earn keeper rewards.

