# Vulnerability details

## Impact
The LybraGoverance contract is inherited from the openzeppelin's GovernorTimelockControl contract, which has a public `queue` function. The `queue` function aims to schedule proposal to the TimeLock contract by calling its `schedule` function, and when the delay is passed, corresponding proposal will be executed. Through the TimeLock contract's `schedule` function has permission check inside, but because the caller is  GovernorTimelockControl contract, so it can be easily bypassed. All in all, the bug is, currently the LybraGoverance contract inherit the GovernorTimelockControl without overriding the `queue` function, which allows anyone to queue malicious proposals to the TimeLock contract and execute it after the delay is passed

