## Impact

An attacker can claim the rewards of any user as long as the isOtherEarningsClaimable(user) condition returns true. This occurs when the ratio of the user's staked LBRLP value (stakedLBRLpValue(user)) to their total staked amount (stakedOf(user)) is less than 500 (0.05 or 5% when expressed as a percentage).

The attacker doesn't need to spend their own funds if useEUSD is set to false when invoking purchaseOtherEarnings(user, useEUSD). The contract burns the biddingFee amount of LBR tokens from the attacker's account but rewards them with the victim's reward amount in esLBR tokens. If useEUSD is set to true, the contract tries to transfer biddingFee worth of EUSD tokens from the attacker to the configurator contract, but the attacker still receives the victim's reward amount in esLBR tokens.


