## Impact
Any address or contract can call this function and initiate a withdrawal.
Since the withdraw function does not have any access control checks, any address or contract can call it and initiate a withdrawal on behalf of any user. This allows unauthorized parties to withdraw funds from user accounts without proper authorization or consent. This can lead to financial losses and compromise the integrity of the system.

If an attacker or unauthorized entity calls the withdraw function on behalf of a user, they can potentially drain the user's funds by initiating multiple unauthorized withdrawals. This can result in significant financial losses for the affected users.

Unauthorized withdrawals can manipulate the account balances of users. Attackers may intentionally withdraw funds from certain accounts to disrupt the normal operation of the system, manipulate the perceived value or availability of funds, or destabilize the platform.

